{\colortbl ;\red0\green0\blue0;}
\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. God from on high hath heard;
\par Let sighs and sorrows cease;
\par The skies unfold, and lo!
\par Descends the gift of peace.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. Hark! On the midnight air
\par Celestial voices swell;
\par The hosts of heaven proclaim
\par God comes on earth to dwell.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. Haste with the shepherds; see
\par The mystery of grace:
\par A manger-bed, a Child,
\par Is all the eye can trace.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. Is this the Eternal Son,
\par Who on the starry throne
\par Before the worlds begun
\par Was with the Father One?
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. Yes, faith can pierce the cloud
\par Which shrouds His  glory now,
\par And hail Him God and Lord,
\par To whom all creatures bow.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 6\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 6. Faith sees the sapphire throne,
\par Where angels evermore
\par Adoring tremble still,
\par And trembling still adore.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 7\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 7. O Child! Thy silence speaks,
\par And bids us not refuse
\par To bear what flesh would shun,
\par To spurn what flesh would choose.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 8\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 8. Fill us with holy love,
\par Heal Thou our earthly pride;
\par Born in each lowly heart,
\par \pard\tx2200 For ever there abide.\tab 
\par \pard 
\par \f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\f2 
\par }

